{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nFollow-up advisories from Gerrit change 2672 patchset 2 identified three cleanup items for the Terraform structural grounding corroborator. Operator ruling 2026-09-08 approved one combined change:\n\n1. Bound peak memory for the sanctioned terraform-config-inspect subprocess. The current `terraform_corroborator._run` uses `proc.communicate(timeout=...)`, so stdout/stderr are buffered before the post-hoc size cap can run. Replace that with incremental pipe reads under the existing deadline, aborting to the existing worker-failure/abstain path when either stream exceeds its cap. Reuse `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` per bug d843 instead of hand-rolled process-group termination.\n2. Remove the dead `_minimal_env` conjunct `and not _drop_env(k)`: `_KEEP_ENV` is a closed allowlist and none of its members match `_DROP_ENV_PREFIX`.\n3. Strengthen match-path non-disclosure coverage so a positive declaration match never leaks the fixture value `SECRET` in evidence or receipt output.\n\nRespect ADR 0115: this remains the single sanctioned Terraform subprocess, with bounded and redacted execution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` reads subprocess stdout/stderr incrementally, enforces `MAX_STDOUT`/`MAX_STDERR` before buffering unbounded output, and reports an abstain/worker-failure result when a cap is exceeded.\n- [ ] Timeout and cap cleanup delegates process-group reaping to `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` rather than a local hand-rolled killpg loop.\n- [ ] `_minimal_env` keeps only the intended allowlisted environment variables without the misleading dead `_drop_env` conjunct.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py` includes RED coverage that fails if the exact-match path leaks `SECRET` into evidence or receipt output.\n- [ ] Verification passes: `checked: env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest -q tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py`.\n- [ ] Final gate passes before push: `checked: env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2`.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788917086429838001,"uuid":"5315975f-eff3-45e9-8407-2f4ab178023c"}